    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d247">

                <pb facs="0251" n="239" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg239"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">845.00/7–2244</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Assistant Secretary
                        of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Berle</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-07-27">July 27, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Sir Ronald<anchor n="27" xml:id="d247-f1"/> came in to see me at my request. I
                    referred to his protest at the publication, in Drew Pearson’s column in the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Washington Post</hi>, of a copy of William Phillips’
                    letter to the President about India.<anchor n="28" xml:id="d247-f2"/> I said
                    this was a wholly unauthorized publication; that we regretted its appearance;
                    and that no responsible officer of the Government had had anything to do with
                    it.</p>
                <p>I added that we were cabling the substance of this statement to our Embassy in
                        London.<anchor n="29" xml:id="d247-f3"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>A[<hi rendition="#small-caps">dolf</hi>] A. B[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">erle</hi>], <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jr.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d247-f1" n="27" xml:id="d247-f1-content">
                <p>Sir Ronald I. Campbell, British Minister.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d247-f2" n="28" xml:id="d247-f2-content">
                <p>Sir Ronald had called and made such a protest on July 25; memorandum of
                    conversation not printed (845.00/7–2544).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d247-f3" n="29" xml:id="d247-f3-content">
                <p>This was done in telegram No. 5933, July 28, 8 p.m.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
